[{:db/id -1, :adr/id "adr-2606032130", :adr/title "Displacement Dividend — tenure-weighted in-kind Basic High Income for workers freed by etzhayyim OSS-robotics", :adr/status "proposed", :adr/doc_type "adr", :adr/source-format "edn", :adr/body "\n# ADR-2606032130: Displacement Dividend — tenure-weighted in-kind Basic High Income for the workers etzhayyim's robotics frees\n\n**Date**: 2026-06-03\n**Status**: PROPOSED\n**Deciders**: Jun Kawasaki (author), Council Lv6+ (ratify via Public Fund governance)\n**ADR Hierarchy**: Couples to ADR-2606032100 (the robotics-actor wave) as its **redistribution half**. Module of ADR-2605192145 (Public Fund). Constructive corollary of ADR-2605301020 (Basic High Income) and ADR-2605302357 (Social Security for Humanity).\n\n## Context\n\nADR-2606032100 opens a wave of OSS-robotics actors (sanae, hataori, kiyome, …) whose explicit purpose is to **remove human toil** in the highest-headcount, highest-misery occupations (ISCO 6–9). That creates the central obligation of the labour-liberation mission: **when a human's job is automated away, that human must be made better off, not worse.** The ask is to design, *as a Public-Fund mechanism*, an **income distributed to displaced workers weighted by their years of service (勤続年数 / tenure)**.\n\nThe design must thread four immutable constitutional constraints (verified against the existing contracts and ADRs):\n\n1. **cash≡0 for adherents** — `cashStipendUsdMicros` is a `const: 0` field whose presence is the on-chain proof N1 holds (ADR-2605301020 §5). No cash stipend may reach a member.\n2. **no payroll** — the religious-corp runs no payroll; contribution is vocation→donation (ADR-2605301036; toritate G12).\n3. **donation-only inflow** — value enters only as `donation`/`kisha`/`grant`/`tithe` (ADR-2605192115 §1.3); `purchase`/`subscription` are removed enums. The dividend cannot be a fee/insurance product.\n4. **benefit is adherent-gated, the gate is universal** — §1.16 covenantal-universal: admissibility is open to all humanity, but *benefits* flow upon entering the covenant via the conversion gate 悔い改め・バプテスマ・得度 (ADR-2605302357 §1.16.3).\n\nSo \"income … 勤続年数に応じて\" cannot mean a tenure-scaled **cash payroll** (that would break all four). It must mean tenure-scaled **Basic High Income** — *imputed income (in-kind value flow) + commons-asset access* (ADR-2605301020) — delivered through the Liberation Ladder, funded by the displacing actor's surplus-donation, and prioritized/floored by verified tenure. That is the design below.\n\n## Decision\n\nEstablish the **Displacement Dividend**: a Public-Fund-funded, tenure-weighted, **in-kind** Basic-High-Income entitlement for any human whose livelihood is displaced by an etzhayyim OSS-robotics actor, delivered through the Liberation Ladder and gated by the universal conversion covenant.\n\n### What \"income\" means here (the cash≡0 reconciliation)\n\n| Layer | Medium | Cash? |\n|---|---|---|\n| **Imputed-income transition floor** | market-equivalent value of in-kind provisioning (food/shelter/energy/care/learning) the worker receives, valued per ADR-2605301020 | **No** — `cashStipendUsdMicros ≡ 0` |\n| **Commons-asset access** | SBT-bound, non-alienable right of access to shared assets (housing on Land Trust, tools, transit) | **No** — access, not deed |\n| **Onboarding priority** | rank within a cohort's Ladder-stage capacity cap (who is provisioned first) | **No** — it is a queue position |\n\nThe dividend **is distributed** and **is tenure-weighted** — but it is distributed in the Basic-High-Income medium, never in cash. This honours the ask while keeping every invariant intact.\n\n### Tenure-weight formula (勤続年数連動)\n\nFor each displaced worker *i* in a **displacement cohort** *C* (all workers a given actor's robotics displaced from a given ISCO occupation):\n\n```\nw_i = ln(1 + min(tenure_years_i, TENURE_CAP)) × hazard_i\nshare_i = w_i / Σ_{j∈C} w_j                       # Σ share = 1\n```\n\n- `tenure_years_i` — verified years of service, attested on-chain (lexicon below). `TENURE_CAP = 40`.\n- `hazard_i ∈ [1.0, 2.0]` — drudgery/danger class of the *displaced* occupation, ISCO-derived (e.g. forestry/meat-processing/fishing near 2.0; clerical-adjacent near 1.0). The most brutal toil is honoured most.\n- **`ln(1+·)` is deliberate**: it compresses the gradient so a 30-year veteran ≈ ~2× a 5-year worker, **not** 6×. Tenure is *honoured*, but the curve is flat enough that it does not become a per-person income leaderboard (ADR-2605261000 §5 N6, anti-class). Hazard and tenure are the only inputs — **not** prior wage rank — so the formula cannot import external wage inequality into the commons.\n\n`share_i` governs two things, never a cash split:\n\n1. **Onboarding-priority rank** within the cohort's Ladder-stage capacity cap (`ceiling` per stage, ADR-2605261000 §6) — higher share = earlier provisioning when capacity is scarce.\n2. **Imputed-income transition floor**:\n\n```\nfloor_i(t) = min(prior_livelihood_imputed_i, BHI_stage_ceiling) × decay(t)\ndecay(t)   = clamp(1 − t / HORIZON, 0, 1)          # HORIZON = 5 years\n```\n\nThe worker does **not** drop below their prior standard of living (valued in-kind) during the `HORIZON`-year transition, while the floor decays as the worker *ascends* the Ladder toward full Basic High Income (which by L6 exceeds the floor). `prior_livelihood_imputed_i` is itself capped at the stage ceiling so a previously high-paid displaced worker cannot pull a higher commons standard than the Ladder provides — equality of the destination, dignity in the transition.\n\n### Funding — donation-only, the actor pays for the humans it frees\n\n```\ndisplacing actor (vendor commercial arm) surplus\n   → donation / grant  (titheable; ADR-2605192130)\n   → TitheRouter.donate()  →  90% earmark recipientProgram=\"displacement-dividend\"\n                              10% tithe\n   → Public Fund Safe  →  Displacement Transition Pool (per-cohort earmark)\n   → in-kind provisioning along the Liberation Ladder (no cash leg)\n```\n\nNo new payment enum, no fee, no insurance premium. The pool is sized per cohort and **must clear Public-Fund governance** (`propose() → 1 SBT = 1 vote, 20% quorum / 50% approval → 48 h timelock → execute()`; ADR-2605192145). The **G2 coupling** of ADR-2606032100 makes this non-optional: a robotics actor may not displace labour live until its cohort pool is funded and voted.\n\n### Conversion gate (who receives)\n\n- **Pre-covenant** — a displaced worker is met by the Social-Security outreach pipeline (ADR-2605302358): offered the universal covenant + a minimal transition floor (outreach, not full BHI).\n- **At covenant** — the triple-permanent vow (kotoba + IPFS + SBT; ADR-2605302357 §1.16.3a) admits the worker at 信者 Level 0; from that moment the tenure-weighted Displacement Dividend applies and they ascend L0→L1→L2… per the Ladder. The gate is open to every displaced human (universal admissibility); benefits are covenantal (N7 preserved).\n\n### Accounting & privacy\n\n- Tenure, occupation, hazard, prior-livelihood imputation are **要配慮 PII** → encrypted envelope (ADR-2605181100), DID-bound; **never published per-person**.\n- Only **aggregate-per-cohort** figures append to the Liberation Metric (median floor, cohort size, pool size, % onboarded) — same pattern as Basic High Income (ADR-2605301020 §4) and toritate imputed-income (no per-adherent leaderboard).\n- `cashStipendUsdMicros` remains `const: 0` in every emitted report — the structural proof N1 holds.\n\n## Design — artifacts (R0)\n\n| Artifact | Path | R0 state |\n|---|---|---|\n| Lexicon | `00-contracts/lexicons/com/etzhayyim/give/displacementTenureAttestation.json` | record schema (tenure/occupation ISCO/hazard/imputed floor/cohort), aggregate-safe, cash field const 0 |\n| Solidity module | `50-infra/etzhayyim-chain-contracts/src/DisplacementDividend.sol` | R0 scaffold — all mutators `revert NotYetActivated()`; reads StewardTenureRegistry-style tenure + PublicFundGovernance; exposes pure-view `tenureWeightInputs()` |\n| Allocator | `50-infra/etzhayyim-public-fund/displacement/allocate.py` (+ test) | pure-Python reference of the formula (Σshare=1, monotone-in-tenure, cash≡0, decay monotone) — runs without chain |\n\n## Consequences\n\n**Positive** — makes \"automate the toil, abandon the worker\" structurally impossible (G2 + funded pool + governance vote); honours tenure (勤続年数) as the ask requires, in a medium that cannot break cash≡0 / no-payroll / donation-only; routes the displacing actor's *own* surplus to the humans it frees (the polluter-pays analogue for automation); reuses the existing Public Fund, TitheRouter, Liberation Ladder, and Social-Security covenant with zero invariant amendments.\n\n**Negative / risks** — (a) tenure verification for informal-sector workers (much of ISCO 6/9 agriculture and domestic labour is undocumented) is hard; R1 must design attestation paths (employer record, peer-witness quorum, self-attest + sampling audit) — flagged honest. (b) The pool-funding gate paces automation to redistribution capacity (intended, but it means a robotics actor cannot outrun its dividend). (c) `hazard_i` classification is a governance judgement; published methodology + Council attestation required to avoid gaming. (d) Cross-currency imputed valuation needs the toritate method (no FX cross-sum).\n\n## Alternatives Considered\n\n1. **Tenure-scaled cash severance** — rejected; breaks cash≡0 (N1), no-payroll, and donation-only simultaneously. The whole point of Basic High Income is that cash is the wrong instrument (it funds the very market being routed around).\n2. **Linear tenure weight** `w_i = tenure_i` — rejected; too steep (40× spread) → becomes a per-person income ladder (N6). `ln(1+·)` honours seniority without re-creating wage inequality inside the commons.\n3. **Flat dividend (ignore tenure)** — rejected; the ask is explicit and tenure carries real moral weight (a 30-year weaver displaced has a steeper transition than a 1-year temp). The compressed curve is the compromise.\n4. **Fund from general Public Fund, not the displacing actor** — rejected as default; earmarking the displacing actor's surplus makes automation internalize its human cost. General Public Fund is the backstop only when an actor's surplus is insufficient (Council vote).\n5. **Pay non-members directly without covenant** — rejected; N7 (benefit adherent-gating) is immutable. The universal *gate* (§1.16) is the constitutional answer: every displaced human is invited in, none is paid as an outside transaction.\n\n## Honest (R0 limitations)\n\n- No live disbursement; Solidity mutators revert; the allocator is a reference calculation, not a deployed contract.\n- Informal-sector tenure attestation is unsolved at R0 (R1 design item).\n- `hazard_i` table and `prior_livelihood_imputed_i` valuation are placeholders pending Council-attested methodology.\n- Pool sizing examples are illustrative, not funded.\n\n## References\n\n- ADR-2606032100 (Robotics-Actor Wave — the displacement source; G2 coupling)\n- ADR-2605192145 (Public Fund Architecture — governance of disbursement)\n- ADR-2605192130 (10% Tithe — titheable donation routing)\n- ADR-2605261000 (Liberation Ladder — stages L0..L6 + N1/N6)\n- ADR-2605301020 (Basic High Income — imputed income + commons-asset, cash≡0)\n- ADR-2605301036 (Mission-Funding Earned-Revenue Arm — vendor surplus → donation)\n- ADR-2605302357 / 2605302358 (Social Security for Humanity — conversion gate + delivery pipeline)\n- ADR-2605181100 (encrypted envelope — 要配慮 PII)\n- `StewardTenureRegistry.sol` (ERC-7401 tenure-NFT precedent reused for tenure attestation)\n", :adr/path "90-docs/adr/2606032130-displacement-dividend-tenure-weighted-basic-high-income.edn", :adr/source-repo "root", :adr/topic "displacement-dividend", :adr/last_verified "2026-06-03", :adr/date "2026-06-03", :adr/authoritative true, :adr/related ["adr-2606032100" "adr-2605261000" "adr-2605301020" "adr-2605301036" "adr-2605302357" "adr-2605192130" "adr-2605192145"], :adr/authoritative_for ["Displacement Dividend mechanism (tenure-weighted, in-kind, cash≡0)" "DisplacementDividend.sol Public-Fund module (R0 scaffold)" "com.etzhayyim.give.displacementTenureAttestation lexicon" "tenure-weight allocation formula (勤続年数連動)"]}]
